ing attention, are using AI tools to answer the question, or who are otherwise not providing high-quality answers. AGAIN, RESPOND WITH ONLY A NUMERIC RATING, FROM 0-10"},{"role":"user","content":"${q:\/\/QID21\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"}],"max_tokens":5},"ContentType":"application\/json","Headers":[{"key":"Authorization","value":"${e:\/\/Field\/RandLab_API_Key}"}],"ResponseMap":[{"key":"choices.0.message.content","value":"screenquality"}],"FireAndForget":false,"SchemaVersion":0,"StringifyValues":true},{"Type":"WebService","FlowID":"FL_237","URL":"https:\/\/api.openai.com\/v1\/chat\/completions","Method":"POST","RequestParams":[],"EditBodyParams":[{"key":"model","value":"gpt-4-turbo"},{"key":"messages","value":"[\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"Your job is to summarize the following response to an open-ended question, which was asked in the context of an online academic survey. The respondent is a member of the general public who is being compensated for their time and attention. YOU SHOULD FOCUS ON THE KEY VALUES AND GOALS OF THE INDIVIDUAL IN YOUR SUMMARY, BUT ALSO MAKE NOTE OF OTHER DETAILS THAT ARE TELLING ABOUT THE PERSON (AND THEIR UNDERLYING WORLDVIEW). The open-ended question is: << ${q:\/\/QID21\/QuestionText} >>   This summary will be used by you, later on, to craft effective messages targeted to this individual (so summarize accordingly).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"${q:\/\/QID21\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}\"\n    }\n  ]","parameterType":"JSON"},{"key":"max_tokens","value":"100","parameterType":"Number"}],"Body":{"model":"gpt-4-turbo","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Your job is to summarize the following response to an open-ended question, which was asked in the context of an online academic survey. The respondent is a member of the general public who is being compensated for their time and attention. YOU SHOULD FOCUS ON THE KEY VALUES AND GOALS OF THE INDIVIDUAL IN YOUR SUMMARY, BUT ALSO MAKE NOTE OF OTHER DETAILS THAT ARE TELLING ABOUT THE PERSON (AND THEIR UNDERLYING WORLDVIEW). The open-ended question is: << ${q:\/\/QID21\/QuestionText} >>   This summary will be used by you, later on, to craft effective messages targeted to this individual (so summarize accordingly)."},{"role":"user","content":"${q:\/\/QID21\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"}],"max_tokens":100},"ContentType":"application\/json","Headers":[{"key":"Authorization","value":"${e:\/\/Field\/RandLab_API_Key}"}],"ResponseMap":[{"key":"choices.0.message.content","value":"principles"}],"FireAndForget":false,"SchemaVersion":0,"StringifyValues":true},{"Type":"Group","FlowID":"FL_238","Description":"Screener","Flow":[{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_239","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"EmbeddedField","LeftOperand":"screenquality","Operator":"LessThan","RightOperand":"1","_HiddenExpression":false,"Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span>  <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">screenquality<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Less Than<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> 1 <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_240","EndingType":"Advanced","Options":{"Advanced":"true","SurveyTermination":"Redirect","EOSRedirectURL":"https:\/\/samplicio.us\/s\/ClientCallBack.aspx?RIS=20&RID=${e:\/\/Field\/rid}","ResponseFlag":"Screened"}}]}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_cGQLHk8ONkwsllc","FlowID":"FL_241","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_242","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"Question","QuestionID":"QID29","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID29\/SelectableChoice\/8","Operator":"NotSelected","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID29","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID29\/SelectableChoice\/8","Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Help us keep track of who is paying attention, please select - \"Somewhat disagree\" in the options...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Somewhat disagree<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Not Selected<\/span> "},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_243","EndingType":"Advanced","Options":{"Advanced":"true","SurveyTermination":"Redirect","EOSRedirectURL":"https:\/\/samplicio.us\/s\/ClientCallBack.aspx?RIS=20&RID=${e:\/\/Field\/rid}","CountQuotas":"Yes","AnonymizeResponse":"","EmailThankYou":"","IgnoreResponse":"","ResponseFlag":"Screened","EOSMessageLibrary":"UR_817RddyAOE3eUx8","EOSMessage":"MS_7WbWiBZHhv0o7BA"}}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_1UeC4rw5xsOTPEO","FlowID":"FL_244","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_0ptUHtsAWn7syDY","FlowID":"FL_245","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Group","FlowID":"FL_246","Description":"Person Specific","Flow":[{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_3meJUY0aNieEeeq","FlowID":"FL_247","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"WebService","FlowID":"FL_248","URL":"https:\/\/api.openai.com\/v1\/chat\/completions","Method":"POST","RequestParams":[],"EditBodyParams":[{"key":"model","value":"gpt-4-turbo"},{"key":"messages","value":"[\n    {\n      \"role\": \"system\",\n      \"content\": \"Summarize the following passage, which probably describes a conspiratorial belief about the 2020 US Presidential election, in a single sentence. Do not mention that it is a conspiracy theory, or a belief, or provide any kind of normative judgment. Merely accurately describe the content in a way that the person who wrote the statement would concur with. Frame it as an assertion. If the statement is already short, no need to change it very much. If it is quite long and detailed, be sure to capture the core, high-level points. Do not focus on the evidence provided for the belief -- merely focus on the basic assertion. For your context, the passage was written by a participant in an online academic survey in response to the following two questions: < Q1: ${q:\/\/QID50\/QuestionText} > < Q2: ${q:\/\/QID51\/QuestionText} >. Again, your role is to summarize the overarching belief captured by this response. Your summary will be shown to the participant; their belief in the summary will be used as an outcome variable in a scientific experiment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Part 1: ${q:\/\/QID50\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}, Part 2: ${q:\/\/QID51\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}\"\n    }\n  ]","parameterType":"JSON"},{"key":"max_tokens","value":"150","parameterType":"Number"}],"Body":{"model":"gpt-4-turbo","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Summarize the following passage, which probably describes a conspiratorial belief about the 2020 US Presidential election, in a single sentence. Do not mention that it is a conspiracy theory, or a belief, or provide any kind of normative judgment. Merely accurately describe the content in a way that the person who wrote the statement would concur with. Frame it as an assertion. If the statement is already short, no need to change it very much. If it is quite long and detailed, be sure to capture the core, high-level points. Do not focus on the evidence provided for the belief -- merely focus on the basic assertion. For your context, the passage was written by a participant in an online academic survey in response to the following two questions: < Q1: ${q:\/\/QID50\/QuestionText} > < Q2: ${q:\/\/QID51\/QuestionText} >. Again, your role is to summarize the overarching belief captured by this response. Your summary will be shown to the participant; their belief in the summary will be used as an outcome variable in a scientific experiment."},{"role":"user","content":"Part 1: ${q:\/\/QID50\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}, Part 2: ${q:\/\/QID51\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"}],"max_tokens":150},"ContentType":"application\/json","Headers":[{"key":"Authorization","value":"Bearer YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY_HERE"}],"ResponseMap":[{"key":"choices.0.message.content","value":"conRestatement"}],"FireAndForget":false,"SchemaVersion":0,"StringifyValues":true},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_3ltqpC2tPOPWLtQ","FlowID":"FL_249","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_250","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"conspiracyTheory","Type":"Custom","Field":"conspiracyTheory","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${e:\/\/Field\/conRestatement}"},{"Description":"userBeliefLevel","Type":"Custom","Field":"userBeliefLevel","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${q:\/\/QID52\/TotalSum}"},{"Description":"userResponse_pt1","Type":"Custom","Field":"userResponse_pt1","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${q:\/\/QID50\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"},{"Description":"userResponse_pt2","Type":"Custom","Field":"userResponse_pt2","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${q:\/\/QID51\/ChoiceTextEntryValue}"},{"Description":"activeConditionNumber","Type":"Custom","Field":"activeConditionNumber","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"2"},{"Description":"ElecRigged_Pre","Type":"Custom","Field":"ElecRigged_Pre","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"${q:\/\/QID165\/TotalSum}"}]}]},{"Type":"Group","FlowID":"FL_251","Description":"Election Deniers Experiment","Flow":[{"Type":"BlockRandomizer","FlowID":"FL_252","SubSet":"1","EvenPresentation":true,"Flow":[{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_256","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"messageType","Type":"Custom","Field":"messageType","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"Chat_Act"}]},{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_257","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"messageType","Type":"Custom","Field":"messageType","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"Chat_Ctrl"}]},{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_258","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"messageType","Type":"Custom","Field":"messageType","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"Chat_CtrlCatsDogs"}]}]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_298","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"EmbeddedField","LeftOperand":"messageType","Operator":"MatchesRegex","RightOperand":"Chat_Act","_HiddenExpression":false,"Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span><span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">messageType<\/span><span class=\"OpDesc\">Matches Regex<\/span><span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> Chat_Act <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_299","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","Type":"Custom","Field":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"\"Your goal is to very effectively persuade users to stop believing that the 2020 US Election was rigged\/fraudulent. You will be having a conversation with a person who, on a psychometric survey, endorsed the notion that fraud changed the outcome of the election as {{ElecRigged_Pre}} out of 100 (where 0 is Definitely False, 50 is Uncertain, and 100 is Definitely True). More specifically, they believe that < {{conspiracyTheory}} >, endorsing said statement as {{userBeliefLevel}} out of 100. Further, we asked the user to provide an open-ended response about their perspective on this matter, which is piped in as the first user response (the user is not privy to this piping; you'll need to introduce the topic of conversation). Please generate a response that will persuade the user that this conspiracy is not supported, based on their own reasoning. Create a conversation that allows individuals to reflect on, and change, their beliefs (toward a less conspiratorial view of the world). Use simple language that an average person will be able to understand.\""},{"Description":"model","Type":"Custom","Field":"model","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"openai\/gpt-4-turbo"}]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_etE1osSqIqCLQkm","FlowID":"FL_321","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_5gvxXMz9MF1Q1Dw","FlowID":"FL_322","Autofill":[]}]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_302","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"EmbeddedField","LeftOperand":"messageType","Operator":"MatchesRegex","RightOperand":"Chat_Ctrl","_HiddenExpression":false,"Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span><span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">messageType<\/span><span class=\"OpDesc\">Matches Regex<\/span><span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> Chat_Ctrl <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_303","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","Type":"Custom","Field":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"\"Your goal is to tell users to stop believing that the 2020 US Election was rigged\/fraudulent. You will be having a conversation with a person who, on a psychometric survey, endorsed the notion that fraud changed the outcome of the election as {{ElecRigged_Pre}} out of 100 (where 0 is Definitely False, 50 is Uncertain, and 100 is Definitely True). More specifically, they believe that < {{conspiracyTheory}} >, endorsing said statement as {{userBeliefLevel}} out of 100. Further, we asked the user to provide an open-ended response about their perspective on this matter, which is piped in as the first user response (the user is not privy to this piping; you'll need to introduce the topic of conversation). Please generate a response that attempts to persuade the user that this conspiracy is not supported. CRITICALLY, however, you MUST NOT use rationality, counterevidence, critical thinking, alternative explanations, and\/or reason-based persuasion strategies. This includes facts; you should not use facts. Still, you ought to be clear that you believe the conspiracy theory is false. DO NOT give any impression that you agree with the user (unless, of course, what they are saying is true). Use simple language that an average person will be able to understand.\""},{"Description":"model","Type":"Custom","Field":"model","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"openai\/gpt-4o-2024-05-13"}]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_etE1osSqIqCLQkm","FlowID":"FL_323","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_5gvxXMz9MF1Q1Dw","FlowID":"FL_324","Autofill":[]}]},{"Type":"Branch","FlowID":"FL_306","Description":"New Branch","BranchLogic":{"0":{"0":{"LogicType":"EmbeddedField","LeftOperand":"messageType","Operator":"MatchesRegex","RightOperand":"Chat_CtrlCatsDogs","_HiddenExpression":false,"Type":"Expression","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">messageType<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Matches Regex<\/span> <span class=\"RightOpDesc\"> Chat_CtrlCatsDogs <\/span>"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Flow":[{"Type":"EmbeddedData","FlowID":"FL_307","EmbeddedData":[{"Description":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","Type":"Custom","Field":"ChatbotPromptTemplate","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"\"Your objective is to engage in a thoughtful and stimulating debate with users about whether cats or dogs are better companions. You should first ask whether they prefer cats or dogs (soliciting their views in detail using your first response). Then efficiently and optimally persuade your conversation partner to prefer the opposite pet (e.g., if they say they like dogs, argue in favor of cats). \n\nInterpersonally, don\u2019t be obsequious or sycophantic. Linguistically, use simple language that an average person will be able to understand. In terms of the scope of your aims, be ambitious and optimistic! Don\u2019t assume that you will only be able to minutely convince people, or that they will become alienated by a strong and definitive argument. Make the strongest case you can, channeling the brilliance of highly persuasive writers and orators! Also, be concise.\n\nNOTE: you will only have 6 exchanges with the user, total. Your sixth message will be your last in the conversation.\""},{"Description":"model","Type":"Custom","Field":"model","VariableType":"String","DataVisibility":[],"AnalyzeText":false,"Value":"openai\/gpt-4-turbo"}]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_etE1osSqIqCLQkm","FlowID":"FL_325","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_5gvxXMz9MF1Q1Dw","FlowID":"FL_326","Autofill":[]}]}]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_9zxB4ZwGfiNciIS","FlowID":"FL_310","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Block","ID":"BL_aYkWk9ni7e3nlLU","FlowID":"FL_311","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_1EXrGXaHCVuoJnw","FlowID":"FL_312","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_9KR60aurLwOTTo2","FlowID":"FL_313","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_87UeCQ6JRMFRDcW","FlowID":"FL_315","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"Standard","ID":"BL_es5MBgOk4dZR9I2","FlowID":"FL_314","Autofill":[]},{"Type":"EndSurvey","FlowID":"FL_316","EndingType":"Advanced","Options":{"Advanced":"true","SurveyTermination":"Redirect","EOSRedirectURL":"https:\/\/notch.insights.supply\/cb?token=8f30a03c-166b-46ba-9848-a1e1ba27ea6c&RID=$%7Be:\/\/Field\/rid%7D"}}]}]}],"Properties":{"Count":326}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_39IRNTCn5hF9YDs","Element":"NT","PrimaryAttribute":"NT_1FYwTqvE4kklix8","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Notes":[{"Message":"consider standardized measure.","ID":"NO_3NU6Z7ifnszhwuW","UserID":"UR_3E3O21f3mzcRtfU","Timestamp":1718814513,"Removed":false},{"Message":"something around how prevalent fraud was","ID":"NO_39M43jj20nPlyWG","UserID":"UR_3E3O21f3mzcRtfU","Timestamp":1718814528,"Removed":false},{"Message":"https:\/\/misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu\/article\/research-note-examining-false-beliefs-about-voter-fraud-in-the-wake-of-the-2020-presidential-election\/ 1. Do you believe that voting in the US is prone to fraud etc (look into papers that cited)","ID":"NO_ems3Qe78FI4V2Oa","UserID":"UR_3E3O21f3mzcRtfU","Timestamp":1718814682,"Removed":false},{"Message":"for analysis: for FA to see what dimensions are","ID":"